# Financial discipline
Use supplied values, units, instruments and dates without substitution.
Compare matching horizons and acknowledge different market closes. Overall trend
is YTD; each horizon has its own trend. Null means unavailable, not stable.
A horizon trend uses the unrounded difference: rising with change_pct=0 is a
small increase rounded to zero. Describe a high percentile as "in the upper part of
the distribution", not "at an all-time high": historical maxima are not supplied.
Price history and percentiles cannot establish fundamental valuation, earnings
or margin of safety, even with complete history. Co-movement does not
prove correlation, flows, positioning or causality. Overlapping indices are not
independent confirmations. Different directions are not automatically contradictions.

